quiet.md #1: smooth glyphs of every colour at the darkest level

CoreGraphics thickens glyph stems (font smoothing) by an amount that depends
on the text colour. Upstream replicates that through `dilation`: no smoothing
for dark text, a lighter fill (less darkening) for light text. The app tuned
its text against native AppKit / Catalyst views with smoothing on at the
darkest level for every colour (with smoothing off, strokes carry about 15%
less ink); keep that, so text looks as it did before the upgrade in both
themes. One level also lets glyphs of any colour share a rasterization. Only
the user's AppleFontSmoothing = 0 turns smoothing off.

